; A program of a Lathe module image on the BBC Model B+128, the ROM form (lathe/docs/bbc.md,
; "Step 3, as built: the ROM form"): started by a * command of the module, its code banks read
; only in the module's image, its regions in sideways RAM, everything else in main RAM.
; lathe/host/driver/bbcrom.py puts it in the image; lathe/env/bbc-bank.env is the same machine
; run with *RUN (the developer's form), and the objects are the same for both.
;
; This file is the machine. A program adds its own `bank`, `rom`, `place` and `region` lines
; after it (bbcrom.rom_env makes them from the program's bbc-bank.env lines):
;
;   bank WIN N $8n FILE     bank n (1 to 15) of the module, which must be `rom`, numbered apart
;   rom  WIN N              from every other program's of the same image (bbcrom.py checks)
;   bank WIN N $0s [FILE]   sideways RAM slot s (0, 1, 12 or 13): regions; a file only if the
;                           region has constants, which the module copies there at the command
;
; The window starts at $8050: $8000-$804F of every bank are the header and service code of
; lathe/rt/bbc/module.asm. It ends at $BFDF, as bbc-bank.env's. $0700-$07FF hold the command's
; tail and the module's stub while the program runs, and so are left out, as for *RUN.
cpu       6502
zeropage  $00 $8F
code      $1900 $6BFF
data      $6C00 $7BFF
more      data $0401 $06FF
exit      return $0400  ; the start-up code keeps S at $0400 (bbc.KEEP), and ends with RTS
output    raw
define    BOARD 3       ; the BBC (lathe/host/driver/boards.py)
define    PORTS 2       ; lathe/src/sys.lth over lathe/rt/bbc.lth
define    MODULE_SLOT 4 ; the developer's form's slot: unused in the ROM form, which takes the slot
                        ; the MOS gives (rt_bbc), but kept so that the objects are bbc-bank.env's
window    WIN $8050 $BFDF
switch    WIN bank farcall
farcall   rt_bbc
